  "description": "The tick foundation for SetNet: the ITickable / IAsyncTickable contracts, the ITickHost registration seam + ambient TickHost.Current, and the TickScheduler central update loop. Register anything into a named channel with its own rate (Hz) and priority; the scheduler drives them all from one place — 30 Hz movement, 10 Hz AI, 1 Hz housekeeping — with per-channel fixed timestep. Drive it with an internal timer (Start) or pump it from your own loop (Pump), Unity-friendly. Set one MakeCurrent() host and SetNet's game-loop modules (Mobs, Locomotion, Spawning) auto-subscribe. Zero dependencies — the game-loop modules depend on THIS, not the other way round, so SetNet core stays a pure transport.",
